## Android Auto

Bible Alarm uses a single `MediaBrowserServiceCompat` for all Android Auto versions:
- `src/Bible.Alarm/Platforms/Android/Services/AndroidAuto/LegacyMediaBrowserService.cs`

**Why no CarAppService:** Google Play does not allow an app to declare both
`android.media.browse.MediaBrowserService` and `androidx.car.app.CarAppService` simultaneously.
For media apps, the required approach is `MediaBrowserServiceCompat` (declared in
`automotive_app_desc.xml` with `<uses name="media" />`).

Relies on:
- the shared `MediaSessionCompat`
- schedule data sourced from Fluxor state (helpers live in `AndroidAutoScheduleHelper.cs`)

